build: 2026-06-26 v10.76.26 (Selbstheilung — self-healing crash-loop Safe Mode)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notesT: Builds on 10.76.25. SELF-HEALING: the app must never trap you at a black
  screen again. If a launch crashes before the UI reaches a healthy steady state,
  the NEXT launch boots into a minimal "Safe Mode" recovery screen instead of
  re-rendering the view tree that just crashed.
  How it works: LaunchGuard (pure UserDefaults counter, can't itself crash) records
  each launch and only clears it once the studio has been up ~4 s. A launch that
  crashes during render never clears the counter → the next launch is protected.
  Threshold = 2, so after a single unhealthy launch you're shielded — you never see
  a second black screen. The recovery screen (plain text, no engine dependencies —
  the one view that can always render) explains what happened, lets you Share the
  diagnostics in one tap, and has a "Continue to Echoel" button to go straight back
  into the full app. Reviewed launch-safe (ui-state) + Swift 6 concurrency-clean.
  Test: 10.76.26 launches normally? (Safe Mode only appears AFTER a crash.) To see
  it: if a build ever black-screens, just relaunch — you'll land on the recovery
  screen with the crash log, not a black void. "Continue to Echoel" returns you to
  the app.
